        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65650,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In the female genital tract, postoperative spindle cell nodule has been described in the vagina, vulva, cervix, and endometrium {17452257; 3358660; 4055221; 7665149; 11293156}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65651,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Postoperative spindle cell nodule typically develops at a site of prior procedure, within a few weeks after surgery.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65652,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions occur over a wide age range, but typically in patients of reproductive age.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65653,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65654,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Postoperative spindle cell nodule is presumably reactive.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65655,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Postoperative spindle cell nodule is a poorly defined nodule, usually &lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;cm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65656,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion is composed of loose intersecting fascicles of spindle-shaped cells with eosinophilic to amphophilic cytoplasm, in a variably oedematous stroma. A delicate network of small blood vessels is common. In addition, chronic inflammatory cells are typically present both within the lesion and surrounding the periphery, which may extend into surrounding tissues. Acute inflammation is seen if the lesion is associated with superficial ulceration. Mitoses can be numerous. The spindle cells are immunoreactive for vimentin and can show positivity for desmin and SMA. Important exclusions include inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour and desmoid fibromatosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65657,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 316,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:20:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
